Bernhardt Trout and Jefferson W. Tester. Chemical Engineering Thermodynamics, MIT 10.40, Fall 2003, graduate level. [Public programme](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/10-40-chemical-engineering-thermodynamics-fall-2003/) · [Study materials](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/10-40-chemical-engineering-thermodynamics-fall-2003/pages/study-materials/) · [Readings](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/10-40-chemical-engineering-thermodynamics-fall-2003/pages/readings/).

Complete the published graduate problem/examination progression with its actual readings. Deepen open-system thermodynamics, stability, constitutive property models, molecular/statistical interpretation, and multicomponent phase/reaction equilibria. The public programme is not a claim that every required textbook or lecture transcript is open; obtain the assigned edition through authorized access.

The instructors, graduate status, scope and resource categories were checked on 29 October 2026. OCW material uses CC BY-NC-SA with stated component exceptions; external texts retain their own rights. Use the exact dated equations and model domains rather than treating this historical course as a current property-data service. No source files are bundled.

